abolic Disorder:\n  Favours first:  abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature, abnormality of the liver, anasarca\n  Favours second: 2-3 toe syndactyly, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification, abnormal joint morphology\n\nGastrointestinal Obstruction vs Infectious Gastroenteritis:\n  Favours first:  abdominal distention, abnormal rectum morphology, abnormality of metabolism/homeostasis, abnormality of the hepatic vasculature, abnormality of the liver\n  Favours second: abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea, body aches, chills\n\nMetabolic Disorder vs Infectious Gastroenteritis:\n  Favours first:  2-3 toe syndactyly, abdominal distention, abnormal astrocyte morphology, abnormal brainstem mri signal intensity, abnormal epiphyseal ossification\n  Favours second: abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract, ascites, atopic dermatitis, bloody diarrhea, body aches\n\nRelated to Gastrointestinal Obstruction: chronic intestinal pseudoobstruction, duodenal obstruction, functional colonic disease\n\nRelated to Metabolic Disorder: cerebral folate deficiency, constitutional megaloblastic anemia due to folate metabolism disorder, familial isolated deficiency of vitamin e\n\nRelated to Infectious Gastroenteritis: campylobacteriosis, colitis (disease), enteritis\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with nausea and vomiting for the past week → abdominal distention → Gastrointestinal Obstruction\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with nausea and vomiting for the past week → anorexia → Gastrointestinal Obstruction\n  A 55-year-old man presents to the emergency department with nausea and vomiting for the past week → poor appetite → Gastrointestinal Obstruction"}
